{"p":"/chat/examples/custom-text-chat-commands","t":"Custom text chat commands","d":"Learn how to create custom chat commands.","h":"<p><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/TextChatService\"><code>TextChatService</code></a> has built-in chat commands for common purposes, such as muting other players and using avatar emotes. You can enable them by setting <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/TextChatService/TextChatService.CreateDefaultCommands\"><code>CreateDefaultCommands</code></a> to <code>true</code> in Studio's <strong>Properties</strong> window.</p>\n<p>You can also add custom commands using <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/TextChatCommand\"><code>TextChatCommand</code></a>. Users sending a defined command in the chat input bar trigger a callback defined by <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/TextChatCommand/TextChatCommand.Triggered\"><code>TextChatCommand.Triggered</code></a> to perform your customized actions.</p>\n<p>The following example shows how to create a chat command that allows players to increase or decrease their character's size when they input <code>/super</code> or <code>/mini</code>.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Add a <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/TextChatCommand\"><code>TextChatCommand</code></a> instance inside <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/TextChatService\"><code>TextChatService</code></a>.</li>\n<li>Rename it to <strong>SizeCommand</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"data:image/webp;base64,\" /></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Set its <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/TextChatCommand/TextChatCommand.PrimaryAlias\"><code>PrimaryAlias</code></a> property to <code>/super</code> and its <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/TextChatCommand/TextChatCommand.SecondaryAlias\"><code>SecondaryAlias</code></a> to <code>/mini</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"data:image/webp;base64,\" /></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Insert the following <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Script\"><code>Script</code></a> inside <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/ServerScriptService\"><code>ServerScriptService</code></a> to define a callback for the chat command that scales the character's size:<pre><code>**Script**\n\n```lua\nlocal TextChatService = game:GetService(\"TextChatService\")\nlocal Players = game:GetService(\"Players\")\n\nlocal sizeCommand: TextChatCommand = TextChatService:WaitForChild(\"SizeCommand\")\n\nsizeCommand.Triggered:Connect(function(textSource, message)\n    local scaleMult = 1\n    local messageWords = string.split(message, \" \")\n    if messageWords[1] == \"/super\" then\n        scaleMult = 2\n    elseif messageWords[1] == \"/mini\" then\n        scaleMult = 0.5\n    end\n\n    local player = Players:GetPlayerByUserId(textSource.UserId)\n    if player then\n        local character = player.Character\n        if character then\n            local humanoid = character:FindFirstChildWhichIsA(\"Humanoid\")\n            if humanoid then\n                for _, child in humanoid:GetChildren() do\n                    if child:IsA(\"NumberValue\") then\n                        child.Value *= scaleMult\n                    end\n                end\n            end\n        end\n    end\nend)\n```\n</code></pre>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<video class=\"gmedia\" controls preload=\"none\" src=\"g/assets/players/in-experience-text-chat/Text-Custom-Command.mp4\" data-alt=\"\"></video>","kid":{"simple":"Chat commands are special messages that start with a slash, like `/mute`, that make something happen. Roblox has some built-in ones, and you can make your own with `TextChatCommand`. This example makes `/super` double your character's size and `/mini` halve it. It is the safe, modern way to add commands to your game.","analogy":"It is like a secret password at a clubhouse. When someone says the exact word, the door opens and something special happens.","keyPoints":["Turn on Roblox's built-in commands by setting `TextChatService.CreateDefaultCommands` to true in the Properties window.","Add your own command by inserting a `TextChatCommand` inside `TextChatService`.","Set `PrimaryAlias` and `SecondaryAlias` to the words that trigger it, like `/super` and `/mini`.","Connect to the command's `Triggered` event in a Script in ServerScriptService. It gives you the `TextSource` (who typed it) and the message.","Use `string.split(message, \" \")` to break the message into words and check the first one.","The example scales the character by changing the `NumberValue` children of the Humanoid, like body height and width."],"terms":{"alias":"Another name for the same thing. `/super` and `/mini` are two aliases for the same command object.","PrimaryAlias":"The main word that triggers the command, like `/super`.","SecondaryAlias":"A second word that triggers the same command, like `/mini`.","Triggered":"The event that fires when a player sends one of the command's aliases.","TextSource":"Represents the player who typed the command. Use its `UserId` to find the `Player`.","string.split":"Breaks text into pieces. `string.split(\"/super now\", \" \")` gives `{\"/super\", \"now\"}`.","NumberValue":"An object that holds one number. Humanoids have some that control body scale, so doubling them doubles the size."},"example":{"title":"Make /super and /mini commands","place":"Script in ServerScriptService (with a TextChatCommand named SizeCommand inside TextChatService, PrimaryAlias `/super`, SecondaryAlias `/mini`)","code":"local TextChatService = game:GetService(\"TextChatService\")\nlocal Players = game:GetService(\"Players\")\n\nlocal sizeCommand: TextChatCommand = TextChatService:WaitForChild(\"SizeCommand\")\n\nsizeCommand.Triggered:Connect(function(textSource, message)\n\t-- Work out how much to scale by\n\tlocal scaleMult = 1\n\tlocal words = string.split(message, \" \")\n\tif words[1] == \"/super\" then\n\t\tscaleMult = 2\n\telseif words[1] == \"/mini\" then\n\t\tscaleMult = 0.5\n\tend\n\n\t-- Find the player and their Humanoid\n\tlocal player = Players:GetPlayerByUserId(textSource.UserId)\n\tlocal character = player and player.Character\n\tlocal humanoid = character and character:FindFirstChildWhichIsA(\"Humanoid\")\n\tif not humanoid then\n\t\treturn\n\tend\n\n\t-- Multiply every scale value on the Humanoid\n\tfor _, child in humanoid:GetChildren() do\n\t\tif child:IsA(\"NumberValue\") then\n\t\t\tchild.Value *= scaleMult\n\t\tend\n\tend\nend)","explain":["We wait for the `SizeCommand` object you added in Studio.","When a player types `/super` or `/mini`, `Triggered` runs with who typed it and what they typed.","We split the message into words and check the first word to pick 2 (bigger) or 0.5 (smaller).","We find the player's Humanoid, stopping early if anything is missing.","We multiply each scale `NumberValue` on the Humanoid. A height scale of 1 becomes 2 with `/super`."]},"watchOut":["Spelling the alias without the slash. Set it to `/super`, not `super`.","Naming the command object something other than SizeCommand while the script waits for SizeCommand. The script will wait forever.","Spamming `/super` multiplies again each time: 1, then 2, then 4, then 8. Add a limit if you do not want giant players."]}}